  "labelled": [
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C34-01, TASK-AC-C021DADA60B8",
      "text": "A ladder whose rounds nobody has marked yet reads \"No rounds marked yet\" (live count and the log's count), not \"0 of N rounds completed\": nothing stated is not zero; an explicit zero still reads \"0 of N\"."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C60-01, AC-R014-01, AC-R014-02",
      "text": "Undo finish · resume ladder keeps its quiet style, its control height and the small button's own inline padding (`var(--spacing-300)`, so its focus frame clears the first letter); its row gives that padding back outside the box with a negative inline margin (`calc(var(--spacing-300) * -1)`), so its text starts at the rounds-completed count's left edge."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-R013-01, AC-R013-03, TASK-AC-C021DADA60B8",
      "text": "The ladder log asks each movement's next-round amount only once a round is stated (zero included): with nothing stated there is no \"Completed in round 1\" field."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-R013-01",
      "text": "A tap inside the live check-off's selection leaves only the rounds before it (the log tiles' rule), where it used to select through it."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "JOURNEY-012 (readable wrapping), AC-R013-02",
      "text": "A live round tile keeps the read-only tile's declared inset (`var(--spacing-200)`) instead of the Chip's wider inline inset, which broke BURPEE mid-word (BURPE/E) in the three-column grid at 390. Size, type, frame and selection are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-30138C4A2AFF (owner decision 2026-11-16, Decision 2)",
      "text": "At a narrow phone width (22.5rem and below; here 320 px) a round tile's inset is tightened from `var(--spacing-200)` to `var(--spacing-100)`, so the twelve-round grid fits one 320×568 screen before Start (544 px, was 592). The column rule, gap, frame, the frame's own inset and type are unchanged; at 390 nothing changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C33-01, AC-R013-02",
      "text": "A live round's toggle fills its grid cell and starts its words at its top, as a read-only round does, so a row's tiles and round labels stay level when one tile's words fit one line and its neighbour's wrap (a one- and a two-digit timed rung at 320 px). The accepted states' rows hold alike words, so nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C35-01, AC-R012-01, TASK-AC-F3CDA21AC50B",
      "text": "The prescription reads the shared `state/ladder.ts` readings (Review's too): each round is also said in words to a screen reader (visually hidden), live toggles describe their round's work, and the summary line wraps a long word rather than overflowing. No drawn word or box changes for the accepted push up and burpee ladder."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-85F76FF493AB",
      "text": "`askCompletion`: a For Time with no cap is not asked \"Work completed\"; a For Time's amounts belong to a race answered Incomplete, never to one nobody answered."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "AC-R010-01",
      "text": "For Time starts where the race ended and keeps only the athlete's answer (`workCompleted`); with no cap nothing is asked or claimed."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-8FF68F3F5241",
      "text": "AMRAP and For Time save authority: a refused save is kept on the attempt's record and said after a reload; a known row whose richer save failed reopens the block."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-R015-01",
      "text": "An AMRAP asks no per-movement amount until a rounds count is recorded (TASK-015, `partialRoundFor`), so the amrap state's log past its cap draws only the loaded kb swing's \"Weight used\" group (bec4454 drew \"Completed in next round\" for every movement); a recorded count draws each movement's next-round amount, and a changed count clears the amounts and keeps the loads. Labels stay Round 7's."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-C37-01",
      "text": "A load field only where a load can attach (`loadApplies`, the set logger's rule the saved row also applies); a multi-round For Time asks loads only; a distance amount takes decimals; the row's own rule (`movementActualFromDraft`) says in the field what an entry is refused on. No accepted state draws a refusal, a distance or a multi-round race, and every accepted state's loaded movement keeps its load field."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-FB8AF4D9B641",
      "text": "AC-C26-01's exact per-movement group list (a group only for the loaded movement before rounds are recorded) is the drawing above; the form keeps its accepted name \"Log section results\" (R7-3)."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-R011-01",
      "text": "An EMOM's clock caption says \"· Rest\" beside its minute while the block's own rest window runs. The accepted emom state prescribes no rest, so it draws no change."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-8C147E2C148D",
      "text": "The card's \"Log results\" action states whether its dialog is open (`aria-expanded`); nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-339D1096F660",
      "text": "Each movement's typed amount and load are kept on the attempt's own record (EMOM, AMRAP, For Time) and restored after a reload; the gallery keeps nothing, so it draws no change."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-D58939F8E091",
      "text": "EMOM save authority, as the AMRAP's and For Time's: a refused save is kept on the EMOM's record and said after a reload; a known row whose richer save failed reopens the block. Nothing the gallery draws changes."
    }
  ],
  "unintended": []
